# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file and offers a "Cite this repository"
# button; Zenodo reads it when it archives a release.
#
# date-released is the day this repository was first pushed. Change it if you push on
# a different day.
#
# The DOI below is the Zenodo record for this deposit. Once the record is published,
# Zenodo also shows a concept DOI under "Cite all versions"; if you deposit a second
# version later, swap that one in here so the citation never points at a stale release.
#
# license lists both because the code is MIT and the data CC BY-SA 4.0 (see LICENSE and
# LICENSE-DATA). GitHub and Zenodo read this field.
#
# An email address is optional here and this file is public, so none is included.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this benchmark or these scripts, please cite the article below.
type: software
title: >-
  Censoring-aware benchmark and validation diagnostics for human monoamine
  transporter activity prediction
abstract: >-
  Curated benchmark of 2,849 compounds with censoring-aware DAT/NET/SERT activity
  labels, an assay-modality labelling of 14,386 human monoamine transporter records,
  the radioligand stratification of the binding-versus-functional potency offset, and
  the scripts that reproduce every number in the accompanying article.
authors:
  - family-names: Sahin
    given-names: Selim Emin
    affiliation: >-
      Departments of Chemistry and Neuroscience, The University of Texas at Austin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8928-7962"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/SelimEmin/mat-benchmark"
keywords:
  - QSAR
  - external validation
  - monoamine transporters
  - assay heterogeneity
  - censored data
  - cheminformatics
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23144306"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23144306"
    description: Zenodo record for this deposit
